{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go","id":1417727,"title":"So... where did Tamuz go?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-11T16:17:40-07:00","id":1417727,"title":"So... where did Tamuz go?","content":"So, got my paws on the new Lunars after a couple of years of actively avoiding 3E after souring on the KS. It's something that was near and dear to me and so far I'm liking a lot of what I see.<br /> <br /> However... where did Tamuz go?<br /> <br /> (And hi folks, long time no write)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T16:31:50-07:00","id":1417730,"title":"","content":"Probably to the land of wind and ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T18:32:11-07:00","id":1417744,"title":"","content":"What's a Tamuz?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T18:33:59-07:00","id":1417745,"title":"","content":"To your question, so simple, I offer answers, in Triple!<br /> <br /> 1. He\u2019s possibly still there, they didn\u2019t get around to mentioning every elder Lunar from past editions, after all. (Silver Python and Rain Deathflyer also didn\u2019t make the cut)<br /> <br /> 2. He\u2019s been written completely out due to the problematic nature of his character. (Who\u2019s Desus?)<br /> <br /> 3. He\u2019ll make a reappearance in a later supplement covering the region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 10-11-2020, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T20:51:27-07:00","id":1417764,"title":"","content":"I wrote <a href=\"https://archiveofourown.org/works/14435823/chapters/33373395\" target=\"_blank\">some fanfiction about Tamuz</a>, before the Lunars 3e came out, in the format of the Aspect/Castebooks which sounds like you may enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T00:08:04-07:00","id":1417776,"title":"","content":"The general gist I got is he's kind of just not needed anymore. Kind of notable is that the Lunar elders from previous editions presented when they had locations tied with them, kind of had thsoe locations baked-into their descriptions. (ie Raksi with Mahalanka, Ma-Ha-Suchi with the Nameless Lair, Leviathan with Luthe.) That is, the locations they are tied to were kind of introduced with them way back in the day.<br /> <br /> Tamuz, along with Rain Deathflyer and Silver Python, were kind of add-ons to locations that had strong thesis that got kind of lost in becoming Lunar things in the game's later periods (2e in Chiaroscuro's case, <b>Kingdomf of Halta</b> in 1e). So instead of focusing on what might be seen as kind of &quot;heat-taking&quot; elders whose relevance ot locations was retroactive, they introduced new locations that had Lunars baked into them basically. This is kind of notable in Tamuz's case since his entire charecterization in 2e was really more or less well, unique ot 2e. And his original presentation in 1e is kind of obsolete in the way that Lunars operate now.<br /> <br /> He also has some other issues, generally like playing on stereotypes of gay men being misogynists or only being so due to bad relationships with women, and having that be ingrained in Delzahn society is a bit yikes htere.<br /> <br /> Note he probably isn't going to be canonically deleted. But I kind of am skeptical he'll show up anywhere in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T00:37:25-07:00","id":1417779,"title":"","content":"Flowchart:<br /> <br /> Are they woke?<br /> Yes -&gt;They'll be in a future supplement. DONE.<br /> No -&gt;<br /> <br /> Are they PG-13?<br /> Yes -&gt; They'll be a Backer Add-on for a future supplement. DONE.<br /> No -&gt; 3E is going in a different creative direction than 2E: the character won't appear in this edition -&gt;<br /> <br /> How do you feel about that?<br /> -&gt; Good: they're problematic. DONE.<br /> -&gt; That sucks! -&gt; Use the 1E material. DONE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T03:15:52-07:00","id":1417783,"title":"","content":"Nothing more woke and PG-13 than doing medical experiments on the local population in pursuit of a plague tailored to the extermination of your enemies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For my money, Tammuz is just kind of dull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T06:07:15-07:00","id":1417798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417776#post1417776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And his original presentation in 1e is kind of obsolete in the way that Lunars operate now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it's obsolete so much as niche.<br /> <br /> Tamuz basically wants the revolution to be as civilised as possible, if the fall of the Dragon-Blooded hegemony isn't already happening he's just kind of hanging back and hand-wringing over the more questionable methods of his peers. He's got much more of a potential role if the Silver Pact has already won and has to transition from revolutionaries to leaders - where you've got this qualified looking guy who did exactly none of the heavy lifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T07:47:15-07:00","id":1417814,"title":"","content":"Never really though much about it, but in retrospect must admit Tammuz is probably the 1st Age survivor i got less use from.<br /> Damn, i think Gervesin, Nazri and Jaguar got more cameos in Chiaroscuro on my games than him. The Tri-Khan <i>definitely </i>got more, as being a &quot;mere&quot; mortal ruler it's much simpler to set up an effective back-&amp;-forth dynamic between him and an average group of exalts.<br /> <br /> Little sticks to mind beyond &quot;elegant-looking&quot;, &quot;social primary elder&quot;, &quot;the signature changing moon wolfman - no, wait, ain't the caste sigs supposed to be starting PC-tier?! Some other guy then&quot;.<br /> <br /> [Kind of have the same &quot;identity problem&quot; with the dude in 1e Lunars cover, thinking of him as Ma-Ha-Suchi in human form, even though i <i>know </i>it's supposed to be Strength-of-Many...]<br /> <br /> In hindsight, i'm kind of sorry i have so little to say of him in comparison to Leviathan, Ka-Koshu, Ma-Ha-Suchi &amp; others. Guess i'll take some time to tinker with the &quot;secret father of the glass metropolis&quot; some day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-25-2020, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T08:36:15-07:00","id":1417823,"title":"","content":"Tammuz is narratively problematic because he takes agency away from the Delzhan, who, before 2e Lunars, were their own independent people. I imagine he's gone simply because he's a relict of 2e Lunars taking the credit for things that were previously established as their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:37:36-07:00","id":1417838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417823#post1417823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tammuz is narratively problematic because he takes agency away from the Delzhan, who, before 2e Lunars, were their own independent people. I imagine he's gone simply because he's a relict of 2e Lunars taking the credit for things that were previously established as their own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you. Also probably because of the stereotype issue. Plus his name is the Babylonian version of Adonis, which implies that he was once the consort of Ishtar/ Aphrodite and thus probably not 100% gay. Maybe they didn\u2019t wanna tie the Lunars too explicitly into RL mythology by using the name of a Babylonian deity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-12-2020, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T09:42:29-07:00","id":1417840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417823#post1417823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tammuz is narratively problematic because he takes agency away from the Delzhan, who, before 2e Lunars, were their own independent people. I imagine he's gone simply because he's a relict of 2e Lunars taking the credit for things that were previously established as their own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's funny, the Delzahn did have a lunar ancestor/patron back in 1e, the Tamas Khan, except he was a distant, kind of vaguely disapproving but non-intervening (for now) one. Some kind of conflation went on there, though to be fair, i remember the 2e writers still keeping both lunars as separate individuals and occasionally citing Tamas Khan (though as a pupil of sorts and mostly ignored). Incidentally, he also had tribes of dholemen descendants - what is kind of funny in that dholes tend to live in places far more forested &amp; humid than i imagine the plains hugging desert i'd associate with the Delzahn. I might be tempted to replace them with jackals if not for &quot;jackal tribes&quot; being the common epiteth of the tribes of disease-ridden mutants.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tamuz as described in 1e Lunars not only has nothing to do with the Delzahn, but sounds somewhat like a Strength of Many without the clear anti-slavery focus.<br /> The misogyny i suspect evolved from how the relation to his solar wife is described in vague, distant terms and the mentions of potential conflict with her current incarnation over the issue of civilization-toppling, a Silver Pact agenda he's described wholy into, even if doing it with a comparatively softer touch. What, considering that sort of conflict was pretty much <i>par for the course assumption</i> of lunars &amp; solars' relations back in 1ed (even <b><i>before</i></b> 1e Lunars, back into the castebooks, for cryin' out loud!), makes such a take a serious case of flanderization and a kind of toxic one at that.<br /> <br /> All of that said, his beastman form, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saluki\" target=\"_blank\">gazelle hound</a>, would make <b><i>a lot</i></b> of sense for a lunar with ties to nomadic hunters &amp; herdsmen like the Delzahn, much more than a dhole for sure... (Though i find the idea of a Saluki warform pretty adorable and would suspect the actual reason Tamuz prefers using his human form is <i>sheer embarassment</i> at it - and his solar mate's reactions. It would be far from the only silly dynamic between elder lunar &amp; young solar i've thrown in my games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> But still, a little Google help just for reference, or fairer assessment:<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cdnb.artstation.com/p/media_assets/images/images/000/436/215/medium/nephelomancer_kingarthur_galahx.jpg?1560122414\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cdnb.artstation.com/p/media_assets/images/images/000/436/215/medium/nephelomancer_kingarthur_galahx.jpg?1560122414\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cdnb.artstation.com/p/media_assets/images/images/000/436/215/medium/nephelomancer_kingarthur_galahx.jpg?1560122414\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><img width=\"1280\" height=\"1920\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://rickwayneauthor.files.wordpress.com/2019/11/justin-cherry-nephelomancer-kingarthur-galahx.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://rickwayneauthor.files.wordpress.com/2019/11/justin-cherry-nephelomancer-kingarthur-galahx.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=\" data-thumb-url=\"https://rickwayneauthor.files.wordpress.com/2019/11/justin-cherry-nephelomancer-kingarthur-galahx.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> So people might judge &amp; appreciate the elder's warform pros &amp; cons on their own terms.<br /> <br /> Also, it's Tamuz, one &quot;M&quot; only, no correlation with the mesopotamian god intended (apparently).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-29-2023, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T12:10:28-07:00","id":1417865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417840#post1417840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's funny, the Delzahn did have a lunar ancestor/patron back in 1e, the Tamas Khan, but he was a distant, kind of vaguely disapproving but non-intervening (for now) one. Some kind of conflation went on there, though to be fair, i remember the 2e writers still keeping both lunars as separate individuals and occasionally citing Tamas Khan (though as a pupil of sorts and mostly ignored). Incidentally, he also had tribes of dholemen descendants - what is kind of funny in that dholes tend to live in places far more forested &amp; humid than i imagine the plains hugging desert i'd associate with the Delzahn. I might be tempted to replace them with jackals if not for &amp;quot;jackal tribes&amp;quot; being the common epiteth of the tribes of disease-ridden mutants.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tamuz as described in 1e Lunars not only has nothing to do with the Delzahn, but sounds somewhat like a Strength of Many without the clear anti-slavery focus.<br /> The misogyny i suspect evolved from how the relation to his solar wife is described in vague, distant terms and the mentions of potential conflict with her current incarnation over the issue of civilization-toppling, a Silver Pact agenda he's described wholy into, even if doing it with a comparatively softer touch. What, considering that sort of conflict was pretty much <i>par for the course assumption</i> of lunars &amp; solars' relations back in 1ed (even <b><i>before</i></b> 1e Lunars, back into the castebooks, for cryin' out loud!), makes such a take a serious case of flanderization and a kind of toxic one at that.<br /> <br /> All of that said, his beastman form, a <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saluki&amp;quot;]gazelle</a> hound[/URL], would make <b><i>a lot</i></b> of sense for a lunar with ties to nomadic hunters &amp; herdsmen like the Delzahn, much more than a dhole for sure... (Though i find the idea of a Saluki warform pretty adorable and would suspect the actual reason Tamuz prefers using his human form is <i>sheer embarassment</i> at it - and his solar mate's reactions. It would be far from the only silly dynamic between elder lunar &amp; young solar i've thrown in my games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> But still, a little Google help just for reference, or fairer assessment:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdnb.artstation.com/p/media_assets/images/images/000/436/215/medium/nephelomancer_kingarthur_galahx.jpg?1560122414\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So people might judge &amp; appreciate the elder's warform pros &amp; cons on their own terms.<br /> <br /> Also, it's Tamuz, one &amp;quot;M&amp;quot; only, no correlation with the mesopotamian god intended (apparently).</div> </div> </div> </div>So I guess the name is just a coincidence. Cool. Thanks for clarifying that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T12:14:24-07:00","id":1417866,"title":"","content":"We didn't have any particularly great ideas for Tamuz and his relation to the Delzhan so we didn't do anything with him. He isn't explicitly erased from canon or anything. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Flowchart:<br /> <br /> Are they woke?<br /> Yes -&gt;They'll be in a future supplement. DONE.<br /> No -&gt;<br /> <br /> Are they PG-13?<br /> Yes -&gt; They'll be a Backer Add-on for a future supplement. DONE.<br /> No -&gt; 3E is going in a different creative direction than 2E: the character won't appear in this edition -&gt;<br /> <br /> How do you feel about that?<br /> -&gt; Good: they're problematic. DONE.<br /> -&gt; That sucks! -&gt; Use the 1E material. DONE. </div> </div> </div>Raksi, Queen of Wokeness :P<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T13:04:26-07:00","id":1417883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417866#post1417866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksi, Queen of Wokeness :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Raksi who no longer eats human babies?<br /> <br /> It's your art man (and it's good art - best edition of Exalted yet), but don't pretend you haven't removed the more questionable elements from Exalted. You've dialed back and toned down the canon that came before, and in every single instance it's made things less edgy, less explicit, and less politically incorrect. You've not dialed anything up, and I'm struggling to think of anything you've added that's not kid-friendly*.<br /> <br /> You do good work. I like your work. It's not a complaint... But, yes, 3E Raksi is the queen of wokeness. Raksi is a prime example of what I was talking about in the post you sub-quoted. Not a complaint. Not a value judgement. It's an observation of what you've published.<br /> <br /> (In good faith: I honestly don't see how anyone can look at the 3E presentation of Raksi as a strong, capable, female mentor instead of a baby-eating witch and not think the 3E version is more woke. But I'm open to having that nuance explained to me if someone wants to elaborate how 2E Raksi is actually more woke.)<br /> <br /> *Actually, I guess Sesus E is more problematic from the whole He-Man Woman Haters Club angle than Tamuz.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417866#post1417866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We didn't have any particularly great ideas for Tamuz and his relation to the Delzhan so we didn't do anything with him. He isn't explicitly erased from canon or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, that's good to know. I appriecate when y'all take the time to explain decisions like this, thanks.<br /> <br /> Any chance of him getting a cameo mention (perhaps as a gay elder Lunar) in Many Faced Strangers? I'm not saying it's strictly neccessary or anything, just that if you don't have an interesting vision to justify a full write-up, a cameo helps the community see which characters aren't in spotlight and which have got the Desus-treatment. Obviously, if it doesn't fit then it doesn't fit - but the community only sees what you choose to put out, so just something to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-12-2020, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T13:45:09-07:00","id":1417901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417883#post1417883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've dialed back, toned down, out-and-out erased, and reimagined the canon that came before, and in every single instance it's made things less edgy, less explicit, and less politically incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you complaining that they took parts of Exalted that sucked and got rid of them? Like, out with the shit, in with something that's not shit.<br /> <br /> Yeah, prior Exalted Editions were edgy and talked about allegedly mature things but in many cases it was in a VERY immature way. Having tits out on every page doesn't make you mature, nor does having an alleged tough character who eats babies. That was just &quot;Ha ha look how CRAZY she is she literally eats babies&quot;, it was cartoonish and actually really dumb. So yeah, toss it out. It's dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-12-2020, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T13:48:25-07:00","id":1417902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417883#post1417883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksi who no longer eats human babies?<br /> <br /> It's your art man (and it's good art - best edition of Exalted yet), but don't pretend you haven't sanitized Exalted. You've dialed back, toned down, out-and-out erased, and reimagined the canon that came before, and in every single instance it's made things less edgy, less explicit, and less politically incorrect. You've not dialed anything up, and I'm struggling to think of anything you've added that's not kid-friendly*.<br /> <br /> You do good work. I like your work. But damn, bad take Vance.<br /> <br /> (And if you don't think that your presentation of Raksi as a strong, capable, female mentor instead of a baby-eating witch is more woke... I honestly have no response to that.)<br /> <br /> *Actually, I guess Sesus E is more problematic from the whole He-Man Woman Haters Club angle than Tamuz.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I'm sorry but keep a reminder to be polite to posters, doubly polite to creators, and also remember who is running these forums. If you can't, please leave the thread.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T14:35:14-07:00","id":1417918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417901#post1417901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you complaining that they took parts of Exalted that sucked and got rid of them? Like, out with the shit, in with something that's not shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to answer your question on the assumption that it's a genuine query: &quot;No.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not complaining. I'm stating fact. It's not a value judgement, it's an observation. Nothing I've written is a complaint.<br /> <br /> 3E Raksi is considerably more woke than 2E Raksi.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that's a bad thing. It just &quot;is&quot;. And folks are free to joke about it if they want, but it doesn't make it less true. Folks can celebrate it. Folks can lament it. It's a matter of taste, I'm not passing judgement here -- except to say what I said, which was that Vance and Minton's work on 3E is my favorite version of Exalted.<br /> <br /> (Also, I disagree that those parts &quot;sucked&quot;. It's a matter of taste, and I'd rather avoid calling setting elements that people like &quot;shit&quot;. But that's incidental to my point.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T14:40:08-07:00","id":1417922,"title":"","content":"Eh, why not not make this the edition war in which people talk about... if Exalted were a band and editions were albums, you'd have one set arguing that Third is the &quot;<i>More mature new sound</i>&quot; vs the people who counter that &quot;<i>Hah, 'More mature new sound' is always a just a code word for 'lost its edge and vitality</i>'&quot; (which it, of course, always is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> I don't think in any case Third is particularly less &quot;edgy&quot; tho. - ritual torture and mutilation practicing Backbending Giants of Dis, anyone? (There's probably a cycle here in which the particular things people got massive bees in their bonnet about being 'edgy' in previous editions and complained loudly and vocally about got de-emphasized, but as a whole? Like, I'm not sure you can even *write* pulp S&amp;S genre stuff - which Ex3's leaned into more than previous editions - without a certain degree of gratuitous grand guignol).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T14:47:04-07:00","id":1417925,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Not so much a moderator tone but an observation:<br /> <br /> &quot;Whenever people debate wokeness on the internet and what is or isn't, it rarely goes well.&quot;<br /> <br /> Perhaps a different part of the topic should be moved onto.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T15:46:08-07:00","id":1417938,"title":"","content":"I think Tamuz is a vehicle for several questions Elder Lunars pose:<br /> <br /> How do you lead a loose organization that puts little faith in leadership, more faith in forging your own way, hard lessons included?<br /> How does an Exalt handle the transition between Castes, between ages, between being an honored second to a hunted Anathema with class and dignity?<br /> What is an acceptable set of lessons to implement in societies you influence from the Solar's failure to rule justly in the First Age?<br /> <br /> We can of course watch Tamuz not succeed at good answers to any of this, and have the players forge their own opinions from his failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T16:19:12-07:00","id":1417945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417866#post1417866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We didn't have any particularly great ideas for Tamuz and his relation to the Delzhan so we didn't do anything with him. He isn't explicitly erased from canon or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, wasn't sure what the deal was with him. He's a character that changed a lot through the editions so I was curious what the take would be on him in 3E. His casual misogyny aside(*), he was a rarely sensible and effective lunar elder without insane plans and tied to one of the coolest nations harkening back to Scavanger Sons. It made him a good ally, mentor and even someone capable of taking a look at the bigger picture.<br /> <br /> I don't envy you having to revamp all the elders, it's one of those things where so many people have their own images of those people that noone will ever be happy with the &quot;new and improved&quot; version.<br /> <br /> * Considering that he went from a lost puppy waiting for his long lost queen in 1E to the 2E interpretation I can easily imagine another change for 3E<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T17:53:11-07:00","id":1417959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417883#post1417883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance of him getting a cameo mention (perhaps as a gay elder Lunar) in Many Faced Strangers? I'm not saying it's strictly neccessary or anything, just that if you don't have an interesting vision to justify a full write-up, a cameo helps the community see which characters aren't in spotlight and which have got the Desus-treatment. Obviously, if it doesn't fit then it doesn't fit - but the community only sees what you choose to put out, so just something to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, it's not just &quot;needs an interesting vision&quot;; we namedrop characters all the time. When a character's previous portrayals have issues that complicate their presentation, then a cameo that fails to resolve those issues is asking for trouble. If we write anything Tamuz in 3e, it will be with sufficient substance to address those issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T18:08:35-07:00","id":1417962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417945#post1417945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool, wasn't sure what the deal was with him. He's a character that changed a lot through the editions so I was curious what the take would be on him in 3E. His casual misogyny aside(*), he was a rarely sensible and effective lunar elder without insane plans and tied to one of the coolest nations harkening back to Scavanger Sons. It made him a good ally, mentor and even someone capable of taking a look at the bigger picture.<br /> <br /> I don't envy you having to revamp all the elders, it's one of those things where so many people have their own images of those people that noone will ever be happy with the &quot;new and improved&quot; version.<br /> <br /> * Considering that he went from a lost puppy waiting for his long lost queen in 1E to the 2E interpretation I can easily imagine another change for 3E<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry for being an asinine grump, but that's definitely not what i got from his portrayal in my recent reading of 1e Lunars. His focus is very much on his project of a tribe/cult/guerilla dedicated to a nearly bloodless toppling of civilization in the South as a whole. His feelings for his solar wife are barely adressed, the focus being more in his &quot;compassion for all people&quot;, with a focus in &quot;patrolling&quot; of the old kingdom and current &quot;soft warlord&quot;surgical strike actions.<br /> <br /> While i don't dislike the &quot;city father in Lunar form&quot; 2e portrayal per se, must admit the &quot;humanitarian nemesis of civilization&quot; of 1e catches my fancy at present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-25-2020, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T18:37:24-07:00","id":1417970,"title":"","content":"Each and every one of the Lunar Elders in 1E were &quot;RAWR WE WILL TOP CIVILISATION FOR BARBARISM IS THE WAY&quot;. You kinda filter that bit out figuring out that it leads nowhere and stinks of colonialist concepts of culture and barbarism. There are 6 paragraphs about Tamuz*, two of those speak of his relationship with his wife, how he took care of her kingdom and how he is now unsure and questioning himself how he will act when she comes back (ok lost puppy may have been a bit harsh).<br /> <br /> * who is distinctly not Tamas Khan, a Dhole Lunar who built the Delzhan and now thinks they have grown soft and decadent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T19:57:52-07:00","id":1417982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417970#post1417970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each and every one of the Lunar Elders in 1E were &quot;RAWR WE WILL TOP CIVILISATION FOR BARBARISM IS THE WAY&quot;. You kinda filter that bit out figuring out that it leads nowhere and stinks of colonialist concepts of culture and barbarism.</div> </div> </div> </div>*enjoys playing Lunars like Garou*<br /> <br /> Yes....that's terrible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T20:03:13-07:00","id":1417983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417970#post1417970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each and every one of the Lunar Elders in 1E were &quot;RAWR WE WILL TOP CIVILISATION FOR BARBARISM IS THE WAY&quot;. You kinda filter that bit out figuring out that it leads nowhere and stinks of colonialist concepts of culture and barbarism. There are 6 paragraphs about Tamuz*, two of those speak of his relationship with his wife, how he took care of her kingdom and how he is now unsure and questioning himself how he will act when she comes back (ok lost puppy may have been a bit harsh).<br /> <br /> * who is distinctly not Tamas Khan, a Dhole Lunar who built the Delzhan and now thinks they have grown soft and decadent</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, the process through which Tamuz kind of absorbed Tamas Khan's narrative then spat him out back is kind of head-scratching, to say the least...<br /> <br /> I'd say the paragraphs on questioning, not really himself, but his <i>capacity to convert her</i> to his current civilization-toppling agenda is <b>also</b> quite standard for 1e solar &amp; lunar dynamics. And i'd say <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DefectorFromDecadence\" target=\"_blank\">more favorable</a> assessments of 1e Lunars sensibilities are definitely possible. That and the words used to describe her make it sound like he saw the queen of back then as pampered, sheltered, if not childish even and might end up patronizing any reincarnation that actually opposes him similarly.<br /> <br /> Actually, with Tamuz' 1e take what interested me is how he goes at it from the bits &amp; pieces given, catching the attention of talented individuals in multiple tribes - and civilized groups - bringing them together into his own society/organization that does attacks focused on specific elements to keep it relatively bloodless and break up the engine of corruption/oppression. Overall, it sounds, imho, far more like some guerrilla group, conspiracy/personality cult or terrorist organization than anything like a barbarian tribe/horde/army, choice wording notwithstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-29-2023, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T04:06:20-07:00","id":1418013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417970#post1417970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each and every one of the Lunar Elders in 1E were &quot;RAWR WE WILL TOP CIVILISATION FOR BARBARISM IS THE WAY&quot;. You kinda filter that bit out figuring out that it leads nowhere and stinks of colonialist concepts of culture and barbarism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lilith is described as having decided to wander the Realm again, driven by a relentless curiosity about her reincarnated mate, visiting spirit courts and walled cities alike.<br /> <br /> Raksi is terrifying, but keeps to her own home, even if she sends out raiding parties to bring her more toys.<br /> <br /> Leviathan lives at the bottom of the ocean, and has no intention of leaving.<br /> <br /> Tammuz wants to bring down civilization, but without the all-caps, a distinction that does matter.<br /> <br /> That description there applies to all of one First Edition First Age Lunar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T04:53:56-07:00","id":1418021,"title":"","content":"In my game, Tamuz is serving as a sort of man-behind-the-curtain for the Southern Lunars. The players (4/5 Lunars) have heard his name mentioned but haven't met him yet. They're currently all under the tutelage of Amatha Kinslayer, who - in this game - once studied under Tamuz but has since gone her own way. The players also blundered into and disrupted the scheming of Hathi, a current adherent of Tamuz. Hathi is keeping an eye on the Cult of Tamas Khan, which the players had accidentally shattered in to four major sects. From her, they learned that Tamuz is waiting for the right moment to have a Second Coming of Tamas Khan but is not yet prepared for that - since the original Tamas Khan is AWOL at the moment. The players' actions got the various sects thinking Tamas Khan's return (whether literal or symbolic) is nigh. Hathi is trying to calm the cults down, while Tamuz is out and about, meeting with other Southern Lunars to organize a Plan B in case the Delzahn start conquering without one of Tamuz's Lunars in charge. As a joke, Hathi told the players if they really wanted to help sort this mess out they could go find Tamas Khan. To my surprise, they actually took her up on that and set out into the desert without much of a plan to find a Lunar that's been missing for centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T04:56:39-07:00","id":1418022,"title":"","content":"This thread is wyld for me as a guy who got into the game at the end of the 2e lifecycle. What I've gleaned so far is that Tamuz is a 1e Lunar who is maybe a fancy dog, or maybe that's another guy, who was bi but now is gay because he hates women because his wife was bad or something but now he's not any of that maybe. He made the Delzhani civilization but now he doesn't like it or maybe he doesn't like all of civilization as a concept in general and wants to end it but he's a pacifist but not really but actually yes. <br /> <br /> Is there a place I can read up on 1e and 2e lore without buying old pdfs? do we have like a database of old content up for reading?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T05:43:00-07:00","id":1418027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1418013#post1418013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That description there applies to all of one First Edition First Age Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that before that you have a whole section on the tribes and projects of the Lunars, on the virtues of barbarism and how the silver pact plans to bring down civilisation as a whole. This agenda is set by their elders, even if the specific elders in the book are quirkier than that. Kind of hard not to see the whole thing in the light that's presented 30-40 pages earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 10-13-2020, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T05:49:34-07:00","id":1418028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1418022#post1418022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a place I can read up on 1e and 2e lore without buying old pdfs? do we have like a database of old content up for reading?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, well there were a lot of changes through time. I'd recommend getting the PDF's when they're on a sale. I kinda just go to the shelves filled with Exalted stuff and go through it. I don't think I've touched the 1E lunar book before yesterday in at least 12 or 13 years...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T06:36:50-07:00","id":1418036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1418027#post1418027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that before that you have a whole section on the tribes and projects of the Lunars, on the virtues of barbarism and how the silver pact plans to bring down civilisation as a whole. This agenda is set by their elders, even if the specific elders in the book are quirkier than that. Kind of hard not to see the whole thing in the light that's presented 30-40 pages earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall, the book specifically lays out elders as people who seclude themselves to run their own domains where they hardly ever tolerate the presence of other Lunars except to provide the first stage of mentorship to new Lunars who will otherwise primarily interact with one another. That the philosophy of barbarian supremacism is something developed and promoted mostly by younger Lunars from a combination of necessary adaptations and misunderstandings of divine intent, largely out of control of the eldest Lunars. And that the Silver Pact was not synonymous with Lunars as a whole but a specific (if growing) subset of them that a lot of the isolationist elders (and traditionalist No Moons) were separate from, and they're the ones with the big agenda of the weakness of the Realm providing the opportunity for a new shift in power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T13:28:50-07:00","id":1418087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1418036#post1418036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I recall, the book specifically lays out elders as people who seclude themselves to run their own domains where they hardly ever tolerate the presence of other Lunars except to provide the first stage of mentorship to new Lunars who will otherwise primarily interact with one another. That the philosophy of barbarian supremacism is something developed and promoted mostly by younger Lunars from a combination of necessary adaptations and misunderstandings of divine intent, largely out of control of the eldest Lunars. And that the Silver Pact was not synonymous with Lunars as a whole but a specific (if growing) subset of them that a lot of the isolationist elders (and traditionalist No Moons) were separate from, and they're the ones with the big agenda of the weakness of the Realm providing the opportunity for a new shift in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the freelancers who chimed in about it back in the day were anything to go on, there was an awful lot of &quot;read between the lines&quot; going on with E:tL. All of the elder entries were basically a past tense of what they had been doing, and the book and chapter intro fiction was a tentative roadmap of where they were going, when present (obviously, the Second Breath of Red Jaws has nothing to do about elders, and then, not all elders got those bits). That might partially explain why the book was so much shorter than the other hardbacks, as any explicit directions were utterly absent. And that, of course, wasn't even the most aggravating thing about the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T14:34:34-07:00","id":1418096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1417883#post1417883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksi who no longer eats human babies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll admit I haven\u2019t downloaded the general release yet but this non-baby-eating Raksi of which you speak is definitely not in the backer PDF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T18:31:33-07:00","id":1418128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1418022#post1418022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is wyld for me as a guy who got into the game at the end of the 2e lifecycle. What I've gleaned so far is that Tamuz is a 1e Lunar who is maybe a fancy dog, or maybe that's another guy, who was bi but now is gay because he hates women because his wife was bad or something but now he's not any of that maybe. He made the Delzhani civilization but now he doesn't like it or maybe he doesn't like all of civilization as a concept in general and wants to end it but he's a pacifist but not really but actually yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, let me sum up some of the bits i gleaned from the editions and try to organize them:<br /> <br /> - Tamuz had a fancy dog beastform in 1e and that description that has stayed the same through 2e, though neither edition talked much of it.<br /> <br /> - There exists <b>another </b>Lunar called Tamas Khan, who is the actual ancestor/patron of the Delzahn people. While not outright eliminating him, 2e relegated him to a position of satelite/one-time proxy of Tamuz, pretty much transfering the connection with the people for the older Lunar. Tamas Khan in 2e was a footnote and you'd be excused for not knowing he ever existed.<br /> <br /> - Unlike 2e Tamuz, 1e Tamas Khan had a more ambivalent relationship with the directions the Delzahn had taken since the takeover of Chiaroscuro. Beside the Delzahn of the plains, Tamas Khan had a more hands-on association with his dholemen children. It was definitely <b><i>not </i></b>his pet project of civilization-building/social engineering.<br /> <br /> - No real discussion of Tamuz' sexual orientation existed in 1e, that being wholy a product of writers in 2e's creative run, though inspired in what i would peg as a <b><i>very</i></b> particular reading of bits on his solar wife from his 1e short write-up.<br /> <br /> - Tamuz' 1e &quot;gimmick&quot; so to speak, instead of a connection as secret patron to Chiaroscuro and the Delzahn, was being a &quot;compassionate&quot; civilization toppling overlord, dedicated to convert people from many walks in life, barbarian and civilized, to his line of thinking and eventual elimination of all empires, through in as bloodless/merciful a manner as possible. While he does not judge &quot;civilized&quot; people as inherently inferior or degenerate, he does appear to see civilization as something of a corrupting influence that must eventually go. While i compared his &quot;one tribe&quot; with guerilla and terrorist groups, it has also dawned me that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nonviolent_resistance\" target=\"_blank\">other </a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-governmental_organization\" target=\"_blank\">possible </a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commune\" target=\"_blank\">paths </a>might also fit under the umbrella of his narrative.<br /> <br /> I'll also be the first to admit this is my particular (re)reading of his 1e write-up, one that others might or not see eye to eye with. And either way has little to no relation to any direction being taken with Tamuz in 3e afaik, as up to this point i have not yet read Fangs at the Gate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1418022#post1418022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a place I can read up on 1e and 2e lore without buying old pdfs? do we have like a database of old content up for reading?</div> </div> </div> </div>The White Wolf Wiki perhaps? No idea if it also covers Exalted materials or not, though i hope so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-13-2020, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:53:18-07:00","id":1418382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1418096#post1418096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ll admit I haven\u2019t downloaded the general release yet but this non-baby-eating Raksi of which you speak is definitely not in the backer PDF.</div> </div> </div> </div>The final version does not specify babies as being the people she eats, because that ended up pulling too much focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T15:05:23-07:00","id":1418435,"title":"","content":"I suppose I could see some ways in which Raksi comes off as better.<br /> <br /> After all, she never cheats, she never bribes, she never schemes, she never lies.<br /> <br /> And that wasn't a lie when she said just now that she never lies, 'cause she never lies.<br /> <br /> And she never laughs when children cry. And she never poisons enemies of mine.<br /> <br /> And she never cries when she's alone at night, 'cause she's not sad, she loves her life!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T15:45:41-07:00","id":1418445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1418128#post1418128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, let me sum up some of the bits i gleaned from the editions and try to organize them:<br /> <br /> - Tamuz had a fancy dog beastform in 1e and that description that has stayed the same through 2e, though neither edition talked much of it.<br /> <br /> - There exists <b>another </b>Lunar called Tamas Khan, who is the actual ancestor/patron of the Delzahn people. While not outright eliminating him, 2e relegated him to a position of satelite/one-time proxy of Tamuz, pretty much transfering the connection with the people for the older Lunar. Tamas Khan in 2e was a footnote and you'd be excused for not knowing he ever existed.<br /> <br /> - Unlike 2e Tamuz, 1e Tamas Khan had a more ambivalent relationship with the directions the Delzahn had taken since the takeover of Chiaroscuro. Beside the Delzahn of the plains, Tamas Khan had a more hands-on association with his dholemen children. It was definitely <b><i>not </i></b>his pet project of civilization-building/social engineering.<br /> <br /> - No real discussion of Tamuz' sexual orientation existed in 1e, that being wholy a product of writers in 2e's creative run, though inspired in what i would peg as a <b><i>very</i></b> particular reading of bits on his solar wife from his 1e short write-up.<br /> <br /> - Tamuz' 1e &quot;gimmick&quot; so to speak, instead of a connection as secret patron to Chiaroscuro and the Delzahn, was being a &quot;compassionate&quot; civilization toppling overlord, dedicated to convert people from many walks in life, barbarian and civilized, to his line of thinking and eventual elimination of all empires, through in as bloodless/merciful a manner as possible. While he does not judge &quot;civilized&quot; people as inherently inferior or degenerate, he does appear to see civilization as something of a corrupting influence that must eventually go. While i compared his &quot;one tribe&quot; with guerilla and terrorist groups, it has also dawned me that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nonviolent_resistance\" target=\"_blank\">other </a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-governmental_organization\" target=\"_blank\">possible </a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commune\" target=\"_blank\">paths </a>might also fit under the umbrella of his narrative.<br /> <br /> I'll also be the first to admit this is my particular (re)reading of his 1e write-up, one that others might or not see eye to eye with. And either way has little to no relation to any direction being taken with Tamuz in 3e afaik, as up to this point i have not yet read Fangs at the Gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting his recruitment as conversion of others opens up the possibility of being some variety of messianic religious leader, too. Assuming that this wasn't included in the &quot;commune&quot; link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T14:10:52-07:00","id":1419227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1418445#post1418445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Casting his recruitment as conversion of others opens up the possibility of being some variety of messianic religious leader, too. Assuming that this wasn't included in the &quot;commune&quot; link.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very much so indeed. In my re-reread of him i'd definitely take some inspiration from Jesus Christ Superstar.<br /> Or maybe a more benign version of James Earl Jones' Thulsa Doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T17:26:06-07:00","id":1420185,"title":"","content":"As an aside, has anything been said on Rain Deathflyer and Silver Python, the pair of Lunar secret patrons of Halta, in 3rd edition?<br /> Kind of curious as it partly connects to the backstory of a character i'm reworking for 3rd ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T18:37:14-07:00","id":1420193,"title":"","content":"Those two seem very in the same situation as Tamuz, i.e.- assume unless they are mentioned one day that they never will be because the wider concept they were written as part of was bad civ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T19:40:04-07:00","id":1420198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1420193#post1420193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those two seem very in the same situation as Tamuz, i.e.- assume unless they are mentioned one day that they never will be because the wider concept they were written as part of was bad civ.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, much like with 2e Tamuz for the Delzahn, their gimmick centered wholy in being &quot;the secret lunar patrons of the culture&quot; in Halta, so i can see what you mean.<br /> <br /> I would have to look at them again in MoEP: Lunars, but in retrospect i have to admit they are quite vague and lacking in detail outside of that relation, actually.<br /> And well, while being a lunar facilitates things, it's not really <i>needed</i> to set up the accords with the Raksha or Caltia. Damn, looking into the 3rd ed. bits on Halta, i'd say the Oracle Tree that looms at the heart of Chanta, capital of the Kingdom of Halta, and shares its wisdom with the city\u2019s priests in entheogenic visions, should be explanation enough.<br /> <br /> They were already kind of like Halta's version of the &quot;we need one or two secret ancients behind it all, for reasons!&quot; old VtM trope, in retrospect, but now the more i think about it, the more unnecessary they feel to me, what's kind of bad.<br /> <br /> Feeling a little lost on how to rework them, but at the same time don't want to just erase them, as they kind of connect to a character i'm updating now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-29-2023, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T05:07:45-07:00","id":1420430,"title":"","content":"So if I ended up using Tamuz I'd go back to this 1st edition pre-Delzahn presentation of an older statesman whose a relic of a more civilised time but I'd lean into the flaws of that ideology, in that there's distasteful rumours that he's a quisling who helped the Usurpation to go down because he expected to come out ahead in its aftermath and negotiate peace with the Bronze Faction. <br /> <br /> As for the Haltan Lunars? At the prospect of them coming back I'd mostly question why they were First Age elders because they don't seem to have ever really been connected to anything in the First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T08:10:58-07:00","id":1420479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1420430#post1420430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Haltan Lunars? At the prospect of them coming back I'd mostly question why they were First Age elders because they don't seem to have ever really been connected to anything in the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly. Even if one takes what is said about their import in the founding of Halta at face value - what is i stated previously is far from necessary in 3e - nothing about it requires them to be First Age survivors. In retrospect, making them &quot;patrons&quot; in the same general sense as Caltia, their influence in the formation of haltan society centered in the making of proving grounds that may generate beastfolk and so on could make for an indirect but active role that is more organic and sympathetic as a portrayal of the characters, i guess.<br /> <br /> But on the matter of the duo's age, i dare say the tale of Amphere in Kingdom of Halta, of how Silver Python took the young proto-haltan lunar of that name under his tutelage and bungled up <b><i>big time</i></b> with the mentoring, resulting in her death and the making of the Shade Tiger &amp; Silver Child seems to run counter to the idea of Silver Python as a very experienced lunar, at least where it comes to mentoring, imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-27-2020, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T00:12:58-07:00","id":1420625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417727-so-where-did-tamuz-go?p=1420430#post1420430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Haltan Lunars? At the prospect of them coming back I'd mostly question why they were First Age elders because they don't seem to have ever really been connected to anything in the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>The connection\u2019s pretty obvious to me: they were relevant and important, both of which qualities were FAA in 2e. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}